Johnston Engineering is pleased to submit this proposal for engineering design and build of a Containerized system with Mixer / Settlers and Electrolyzer. 

# Intro: 

Johnston Engineering (JE) is a mechanical engineering firm located in Spokane, Washington **specializing in the design, analysis, integration, ****build****, and testing of first-of-a-kind systems**. In operation since 2015, JE brings over 250 years of combined engineering experience across a team of 23, with deep expertise in product development, system integration and advanced engineering solutions. Our work spans material recovery and electrochemical systems, industrial machinery, as well as clean technology sectors including carbon capture, hydrogen, nuclear, and long-duration energy storage.

JE utilizes an “*analysis-driven design**”* approach, meaning **a****t JE**** y****our designers are also ****your ****analysts****. **Using SolidWorks 3D CAD and ANSYS Finite Element Analysis (FEA)and Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD), our team excels in component modeling, full system integration, and physics-based simulations of thermal, structural and fluid-flow analysis. This closely integrated coupling of design and analysis ensures that system performance is validated before fabrication begins, reducing risk and accelerating development. 

At JE your designers are also your builders. The same engineers who model and analyze the system are also in charge of fabrication oversight, procurement, assembly, and testing. This continuity produces engineers with a uniquely deep understanding of the design intent, system behavior, and how the system is installed in the real world.

To date, JE has completed over 190 first-of-a-kind engineering projects for various clients and 29 projects with the Department of Energy (DOE). Our focus on FOAK development, combined with our integrated design-analysis-build-test approach, makes Johnston Engineering an ideal partner for scale-up and deployment of the Containerized system with Mixer / Settlers and Electrolyzer.

# Scope:

Johnston Engineering will provide mechanical, electrical, and software engineering services to support the design, analysis, fabrication, and testing of the Containerized system with Mixer / Settlers and Electrolyzer. The system is intended to test a new reaction process.  The input into the cathode of the electrolyzer is an aqueous mixture of organic matter that passes through two stages of mixer settlers.  The anode side of the electrolyzer is fed from a third mixer / settler.  Our engineering support is intended to advance the system through all phases necessary for functional deployment, including hardware integration and controls development.  A high-level process flow diagram is shown below in Figure 1.

Figure 1 High-level process flow diagram

# Timeline:

Johnston Engineering will deliver a fully assembled and tested system, including all 3D CAD models, 2D fabrication-ready drawings, and supporting analysis documentation. The target **project duration is 4–6 months** from project initiation.

# Key Tasks & Pricing Estimate: 

Table 1 summarizes key tasks and associated costs estimated to design and build the Containerized system with Mixer / Settlers and Electrolyzer. 

We **estimate ****$****1,100,000 ****to ****$****1,285,000**** to complete the ****Scope** on a T&M basis. 

Table 1 Project Task, Description and cost.  

| Task | Description | Labor Estimate | Total Cost with labor and hardware ($) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Electrolyzer | Design of electrolyzer including 3D CAD and fabrication 2D drawings Structural analysis (FEA) Thermal analysis (FEA) Flow analysis (CFD) to determine in-cell flow distribution Hardware procurement Hardware assembly Leak testing | 800 hours | 250-300k |
| Mixer /  Settlers | Design of quantity three mixer / settler including 3D CAD and fabrication 2D drawings Structural analysis (FEA) if needed Hardware procurement Hardware assembly Leak testing | 700 hours | 350-400k |
| Balance of Plant and integration into shipping container | Design: generation of 3D CAD and 2D fabrication drawings. Component layout in shipping container and design modifications to shipping container. Plumbing and electrical system to connect all components Identification and selection of sensors Hardware procurement Secure mixer / settlers and electrolyzer in shipping container Mechanical and electrical system-level build to connect all hardware components together. Leak testing | 1200 hours | 350-400k |
| Controls | Design of controls system, panels, control wiring, writing control system code Fabrication of control system panels, installation into shipping container, sensor wiring Control system initial testing | 250 hours | 100-125k |
| System testing | Control system functionality testing System level mechanical and electrical testing with surrogate liquid | 200 hours | 40-50k |
| Project close out and shipping | Packaging system for shipping and cost to ship unit to Client | 16 hours | 10k |

# Testing & Post-Deployment Support: 

Following delivery, Johnston Engineering can provide installation, testing, and ongoing system support on a time and materials basis. This includes site travel (domestic or international), coordination of logistics, and ensuring all personnel arrive equipped with the appropriate tools, documentation, and training. Our team is prepared to assist with commissioning, maintenance, or any post-deployment engineering support required to ensure long-term system performance.

